<h3>What If You Want to Change the Layout?</h3>
<p class="isSelectedEnd">Changing a layout can range from simple to highly complex.</p>
<p class="isSelectedEnd">Moving furniture is easy. Removing or altering walls is not.</p>

<ul data-spread="false">
 	<li>Non-load-bearing walls may be removed relatively easily</li>
 	<li>Structural walls require engineering input, steelwork, and building control approval</li>
</ul>
<p class="isSelectedEnd">Before committing to structural changes, it is important to understand what you are trying to improve.</p>
<p class="isSelectedEnd">Ask yourself:</p>

<ul data-spread="false">
 	<li>Do I need more natural light?</li>
 	<li>Do I want better flow between rooms?</li>
 	<li>Do I need more seating space?</li>
 	<li>Do I need more storage?</li>
</ul>
<p class="isSelectedEnd">In many cases, these goals can be achieved without major structural work. When structural reconfigurations are unavoidable, reviewing <a href="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/how-much-does-a-design-and-build-project-cost-in-london-in-2026/">how much a design and build project costs in London</a> clarifies early budget allocations.</p>

